-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ח/2 (10.12.2017): ניכוי שכר לעובדי הוראה בשל השבתת מערכת החינוך בשנת הלימודים התשע"ח
-- No pay for strike hours: the owners deduct from teaching employees who
-- struck in school year תשע"ח, by the attendance reports and the hourly
-- value, and the Ministry deducts from its payments to the owners.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר תשע"ח/2 ניכוי שכר בשל השבתה`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 The letterhead, date, reference, addressee, greeting and subject line; no rule.

@desc A teaching employee's part in the strike the teachers' union announced in school year תשע"ח, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `strike record` HAS
    `reported attendance on the strike days`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc reported attendance at the workplace for the strike dates
    `took part in the strike by the reports`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the attendance reports show, where there are reports
    `produced an approval of absence`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc an approval of the absence under the procedures
    `produced proof of attendance`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc proof of presence at the workplace
    `teaching hours missed`                     IS A NUMBER  @desc hours of teaching not worked during the strike
    `stay hours missed`                         IS A NUMBER  @desc שעות שהייה the employee was to perform during the strike
    `individual hours missed`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc שעות פרטניות the employee was to perform during the strike
    `hourly value`                              IS A NUMBER  @desc the employee's hourly value (ערך השעה); the circular does not set it, an input

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct from the salary` HAS `deduction made` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct from the current MTM payments` HAS `payment deduction` IS A NUMBER

-- The government decisions 647 (22.4.80) and 646 (26.5.81): no salary is
-- paid for strike days; in budgeted bodies this follows from section 29 of
-- the Budget Foundations Law.
@ref akn:hc_1/p13
GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary owed for strike hours` `hours` IS 0

-- ¶14: the owner deducts from the salary of those who took part, by the
-- hours they were absent. The circular names no month to do it by.
@ref akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN s IS A `strike record`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the owner's deduction` s IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `deduct from the salary` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `the salary deduction` s

-- ¶15: the deduction follows the attendance reports; a teaching employee
-- who did not report attendance on the strike date, and produced neither an approval of the absence nor proof of
-- presence, is held to have taken part.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15
GIVEN s IS A `strike record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is held to have taken part in the strike` s IF
    IF s's `reported attendance on the strike days`
    THEN s's `took part in the strike by the reports`
    ELSE NOT s's `produced an approval of absence`
         AND NOT s's `produced proof of attendance`

-- ¶16: the hours of absence, stay hours and individual hours included.
@ref akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN s IS A `strike record`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours of absence` s IS
    s's `teaching hours missed`
    PLUS s's `stay hours missed`
    PLUS s's `individual hours missed`

@ref akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN s IS A `strike record`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary deduction` s IS
    IF `is held to have taken part in the strike` s
    THEN `hours of absence` s TIMES s's `hourly value`
    ELSE 0

-- ¶17: the Ministry deducts from the owner's current MTM payments by the
-- budgeted hours in the striking institutions and the strike dates.
@ref akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN `budgeted hours in striking institutions on the strike dates` IS A NUMBER
      `budgeted value of an hour` IS A NUMBER @desc the MTM budget per hour; set elsewhere
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ministry's deduction from the owner` `budgeted hours in striking institutions on the strike dates` `budgeted value of an hour` IS
    `budgeted hours in striking institutions on the strike dates` TIMES `budgeted value of an hour`

@ref akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN `deduction due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's deduction` `deduction due` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `deduct from the current MTM payments` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `deduction due`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and the copies list; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_02-a: ¶15 holds a non-reporting employee to have taken
-- part "in the strike OR the organisational measures", but the duty to
-- deduct (¶14) and its measure (¶16) are for the strike's hours of absence
-- only; for organisational measures the circular gives no consequence.
DECLARE `industrial action` IS ONE OF `the strike`, `organisational measures`

GIVEN a IS AN `industrial action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the presumption of ¶15 reaches` a IF TRUE

GIVEN a IS AN `industrial action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `¶14 and ¶16 say what to deduct for` a IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the strike` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

`organisational measures are presumed but given no deduction` MEANS
        `the presumption of ¶15 reaches` `organisational measures`
    AND NOT `¶14 and ¶16 say what to deduct for` `organisational measures`
#ASSERT `organisational measures are presumed but given no deduction`

§§ `Worked examples`

-- The hourly value of 100 is a placeholder.
`a striker who did not report` MEANS
    `strike record` WITH
        `reported attendance on the strike days` IS FALSE
        `took part in the strike by the reports` IS FALSE
        `produced an approval of absence`        IS FALSE
        `produced proof of attendance`           IS FALSE
        `teaching hours missed`                  IS 5
        `stay hours missed`                      IS 2
        `individual hours missed`                IS 1
        `hourly value`                           IS 100

`a teacher who proved attendance` MEANS
    `strike record` WITH
        `reported attendance on the strike days` IS FALSE
        `took part in the strike by the reports` IS FALSE
        `produced an approval of absence`        IS FALSE
        `produced proof of attendance`           IS TRUE
        `teaching hours missed`                  IS 0
        `stay hours missed`                      IS 0
        `individual hours missed`                IS 0
        `hourly value`                           IS 100

#ASSERT `the salary deduction` `a striker who did not report` EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `the salary deduction` `a teacher who proved attendance` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `salary owed for strike hours` 8 EQUALS 0

#TRACE `the owner's deduction` `a striker who did not report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct from the salary` 800 AT 1
